<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Honiara</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Honiara is the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/solomon">Solomon</a> Islands, on the north coast of Guadalcanal. It grew from the base built by American forces during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guadalcanal-campaign">Guadalcanal campaign</a> of 1942–1943 and replaced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tulagi">Tulagi</a> as the capital of the British Solomon Islands <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">Protectorate</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>, remaining capital at independence in 1978.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/honiara.jpg" alt="Honiara" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kahunapule Michael Johnson from Pukalani, Hawaii, United States of America · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Honiara_View.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
